      <description>&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/admin/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;sami&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/admin/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Sami Domisch&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a Leibniz Junior Research Group Leader and is interested in freshwater biodiversity and biogeography across spatial scales, and in developing tools in spatial freshwater biodiversity science.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/jaime-garcia-marquez/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;jaime&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/jaime-garcia-marquez/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Jaime Garcia Marquez&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a GIS Data Analyst with a strong emphasis in open-source methods &amp;amp; tools for analysing large biodiversity data sets using the Linux command-line and the High Performance Computing cluster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/yusdiel-torres-cambas/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;yusdiel&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/yusdiel-torres-cambas/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Yusdiel Torres Cambas&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is an Alexander von Humboldt Postdoc. He is working on spatial conservation planning across Cuba considering freshwater biodiversity and ecosystem services under present-day conditions and global change scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/afroditi-grigoropoulou/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;afroditi&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/afroditi-grigoropoulou/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Afroditi Grigoropoulou&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a PhD student focusing on global aquatic insect biodiversity, with an emphasis on patterns of aquatic insect diversity across multiple spatial scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/maria-ueblacker/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;marlene&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/maria-ueblacker/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maria Üblacker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a PhD student working on a high-resolution freshwater habitat characterization across spatial scales, to highlight patterns and potential gaps in the global network of protected areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/gabriela-spriestersbach/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;gabriela&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;140&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/gabriela-spriestersbach/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gabriela Spriestersbach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a Bachelor student from the Technical University Darmstadt working as an Intern at the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.igb-berlin.de/en/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;IGB&lt;/a&gt;. She is exploring methods in freshwater biodiversity data processing and species distribution modelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visitors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/mathieu-floury/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;mathieu&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/mathieu-floury/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mathieu Floury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a visiting Postdoc from the Ecology of Natural and Anthropized Hydrosystems Lab &lt;a href=&#34;https://umr5023.univ-lyon1.fr&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;(LEHNA)&lt;/a&gt;. He is interested in ecology and conservation of biodiversity in hydrosystems across spatial and temporal scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/xiling-deng/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;xiling&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.senckenberg.de/de/institute/senckenberg-gesellschaft-fuer-naturforschung-frankfurt-main/abt-terrestrische-zoologie/sekt-entomologie-iii/entomologie-iii-team/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Xiling Deng&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a visiting PhD student from the Senckenberg Research Institute and Natural History Museum. She is working on the phylogeography of caddiesflies along elevational gradients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/francesco-polazzo/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;francesco&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/francesco-polazzo/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Francesco Polazzo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a visiting PhD student from the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.water.imdea.org/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;IMDEA Water Institute of Alcalá de Henares, Madrid&lt;/a&gt;. He studies how climate change and others drivers of environmental change affect the stability and vulnerability of aquatic communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Previous members&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/thomas-tomiczek/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;thomas&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/thomas-tomiczek/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thomas Tomiczek&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; did his master thesis at the Humboldt University working and the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.igb-berlin.de/en/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;IGB&lt;/a&gt;. His thesis addressed integrating freshwater biodiversity in large scale conservation planning in Colombia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/jens-kiesel/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;jens&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/jens-kiesel/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Jens Kiesel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a hydrologic modeller with a long experience in the fields of hydrology, hydraulics, erosion and sediment transport as well as habitat modelling on various scales and ecoregions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/longzhu-shen/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;longzhu&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/longzhu-shen/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr. Longzhu Shen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was a postdoc with a strong mathematical background, focusing on machine learning and GIS methods to optimize predictions of discharge and nutrients in stream networks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/lydia-nass/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;lydia&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/lydia-nass/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lydia Nass&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; did a master internship at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.igb-berlin.de/en/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;IGB&lt;/a&gt;, focusing on open-source geocomputational and species distribution modelling methods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/martin-friedrichs-manthay/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;martin&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;130&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;https://martinfriedrichs.de/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Martin Friedrichs-Manthay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was a PhD student working on fish distribution models, assessing scale-dependencies and model uncertainties for conservation (funded by the &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.glance-projects.eu/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GLANCE project&lt;/a&gt; and co-supervised by Sami).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;













&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;/authors/annika-brunner/avatar.jpg#floatleft&#34; alt=&#34;annika&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable width=&#34;130&#34; height=&#34;140&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 
&lt;a href=&#34;/authors/annika-brunner/&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Annika Brunner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was a master Student at Freie Universität Berlin and wrote her master thesis at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.igb-berlin.de/en/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;IGB&lt;/a&gt;. Annika integrated Shared Socioeconomic Pathways (SSPs) into freshwater biodiversity projections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
